import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — FOLD_OPS: one compile-time fold alphabet; the premise-pay leg flips","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/fold-cost-single-source.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/fold-cost-single-source.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/fold-cost-single-source.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-fold-ops-one-compile-time-fold-alphabet-the-premise-pay-leg-flips" tabindex="-1">Retro — <code>FOLD_OPS</code>: one compile-time fold alphabet; the premise-pay leg flips <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-fold-ops-one-compile-time-fold-alphabet-the-premise-pay-leg-flips" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — FOLD_OPS: one compile-time fold alphabet; the premise-pay leg flips”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-10-19. <strong>Follows</strong>: <code>enablement-floor.md</code> — its named open item: <em>&quot;a cost model that credits compile-time weight folds would flip the measured pay leg — a cost-model gap, not a law-truth gap.&quot;</em><strong>Commits</strong>: <code>ccfb9ba</code> (the change + tests), this commit (retro + GOALS).</p><h2 id="the-gap-was-drift-not-a-missing-model" tabindex="-1">The gap was drift, not a missing model <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-gap-was-drift-not-a-missing-model" aria-label="Permalink to “The gap was drift, not a missing model”">​</a></h2><p>The machinery already existed: <code>dag_cost</code>&#39;s per-node walk, the e-class-level param-only discount in <code>extract_best</code>, and <code>_generic_overhead</code> all consult <code>cost._folds_to_param</code> — &quot;a subtree closed over Param/Const leaves is compile-time work, priced ~0 marginal&quot;, which is exactly the generic principle required (a structural property, never <code>op == &quot;conv2d&quot;</code>). What had drifted was the <em>alphabet</em> the predicate consulted:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>consumer</th><th>fold set before</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>torch_bridge._fold_weight_chains</code> (the truth)</td><td>160-op literal <code>elif</code> + <code>matmul</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>cost._folds_to_param</code></td><td><code>_FOLDABLE_ELEMWISE</code> (13) + <code>_FOLDABLE_VIEWS</code> (14) + <code>matmul</code>/<code>concat</code> = 29</td></tr><tr><td><code>egraph.extract._FOLDABLE_OPS</code></td><td><code>_FOLDABLE_ELEMWISE</code> + <code>matmul</code>/<code>concat</code> = <strong>15 — no views</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The elif list was widened to ~160 ops in the e6a618e semantic-coverage pass and the cost side was never re-synced — <code>rsqrt</code> (the conv+BN scale chain&#39;s root op), reductions, creators, the activation family all missing. Extraction&#39;s <code>_FOLDABLE_OPS</code> was worse: it predated <code>_FOLDABLE_VIEWS</code> entirely, so a <code>reshape</code>/<code>transpose</code> node inside a foldable weight chain billed the whole subtree at runtime — a second, independent drift (<code>test_transpose_spelled_chain_does_not_pay</code> pinned it as intended behavior; it now asserts the honest outcome).</p><h2 id="the-fix-—-one-table-three-readers" tabindex="-1">The fix — one table, three readers <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-fix-—-one-table-three-readers" aria-label="Permalink to “The fix — one table, three readers”">​</a></h2><p><code>opmeta</code> gains the <code>fold-at-lowering</code> tag and the <code>_FOLD_AT_LOWERING</code> membership (161 names = the lowerer&#39;s elif ∪ <code>matmul</code>), merged into the registry at build so <code>ops(FOLD) → FOLD_OPS</code> is the projection. All three consumers read it:</p><ul><li><code>torch_bridge._fold_weight_chains</code>&#39;s <code>elif</code> dispatches on <code>FOLD_OPS</code> — the literal list is gone, the <em>declined</em> family (slice/extraction views) is documented at the data site;</li><li><code>cost._folds_to_param</code> checks <code>FOLD_OPS</code> with the <code>matmul</code>/<code>concat</code> real-operand rule layered on (<code>_FOLD_EVAL_OPS</code> = the shallow-eval residue);</li><li><code>extract._FOLDABLE_OPS = FOLD_OPS</code> — the e-class discount now covers views and the whole widened set.</li></ul><p>60 binding-only spellings (<code>sin</code>/<code>zeros</code>/<code>ones_like</code>/…) register into the vocabulary through the table — <code>validate_aten_map</code> stays clean (additive registration, no shadowing). Semantics preserved: <code>matmul</code> reaching the eval arm degrades identically (eval declines Const/unresolvable args); every newly-foldable op was already folded by the lowerer — only the <em>price</em> changed.</p><h2 id="measured-—-the-premise-pay-leg-before-after" tabindex="-1">Measured — the premise-pay leg, before/after <a class="header-anchor" href="#measured-—-the-premise-pay-leg-before-after" aria-label="Permalink to “Measured — the premise-pay leg, before/after”">​</a></h2><p><code>lab/probes/conv_fold_premise_pay_probe.py</code> on the real eval-mode <code>ConvBN</code> seed (same run, both legs):</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>leg</th><th>before (<code>de72c64</code>)</th><th>after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>transport</td><td>hooks rebuilt transitively</td><td>same</td></tr><tr><td>truth (real site)</td><td>1eq/0ne accepted</td><td>1eq/0ne — unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>truth (premise-anchored)</td><td>derivable, replayable, 2-step cert</td><td>same</td></tr><tr><td><strong>pay</strong></td><td><code>fires=1</code> <code>changed=False</code> <code>verified=same</code></td><td><code>fires=1</code> <strong><code>changed=True</code> <code>verified=pass</code></strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>dag_cost</code></td><td>spelled=34 874.3 vs fused=34 874.34</td><td>spelled=34 874.3 vs <strong>fused=17 438.7</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The fused member now wins extraction by ~2× (the <code>batch_norm</code> eval pass + every spelled weight op priced out; only <code>conv2d</code> remains). The premise-pay floor evidence the retro named now exists: a dependent mint that fires, truth-verifies, AND pays.</p><h2 id="the-guarded-sweep-—-verdict-still-refuse-default-unchanged" tabindex="-1">The guarded sweep — verdict: still refuse, DEFAULT unchanged <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-guarded-sweep-—-verdict-still-refuse-default-unchanged" aria-label="Permalink to “The guarded sweep — verdict: still refuse, DEFAULT unchanged”">​</a></h2><p><code>run_gauntlet</code> over <code>default_gauntlet_corpus()</code> (364 terms / 245 probes / 83 base rules) on the five floor candidates:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>rule</th><th>verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>conv_channel_{scale,scale_l,shift,shift_sub}_sp</code> (4 anchors)</td><td>REFUSED @ <strong>truth</strong>: <code>0 accepted / 2360 envs</code>, <code>derivable=False</code> — the enumeration bank cannot spell the conv channel-view corner, the real corpus has no spelled sites. Same refusal as the earlier sweep — a domain-starvation gap the cost model cannot repair.</td></tr><tr><td><code>batch_norm_expand</code></td><td>REFUSED @ <strong>typed-pay</strong>: <code>fires=8 typed=8 paid=0</code> — spelling BN <em>out</em> adds ops on the corpus sites it fires on; the paying direction is the <em>composite</em> (BN onto conv), not the expansion.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>So the anchors remain <strong>enabled-but-opt-in</strong>: their dependent mint now demonstrably pays, but their own admission still fails the truth leg (guarded-region starvation — the named corner-reaching route is still requirement #1). <code>batch_norm_expand</code>&#39;s enablement account is real (its premise seat in the paying composite) but it pays nothing itself. The minted composite is <code>syn_*</code>-provenance — admission to <code>DEFAULT</code> runs through the machine-admitted law machinery, not this sweep.</p><h2 id="what-stays-open" tabindex="-1">What stays open <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The conv corner-reaching truth route (enumeration vocabulary for <code>conv2d</code>/channel-views or witness-driven sites) — unchanged.</li><li><code>run_gauntlet</code>/<code>pl.measure</code> on guarded minted composites still does not terminate in the box (the 83-rule <code>_reach</code>/derivability saturation) — the composite was admitted via the bounded probe stages, not the full gauntlet.</li><li><code>FOLD_OPS</code> is the <em>torch lowering&#39;s</em> contract; another backend (ONNX sink, CUDA runner) folding differently would need its own alphabet — the tag&#39;s docstring scopes it accordingly.</li><li>Pre-existing suite finding (not this change&#39;s): <code>test_every_conditional_rule_is_swept</code> counts 125 conditional rules vs the pinned 124 — a stale pin at HEAD, verified failing on clean <code>main</code> before this commit.</li></ul><h2 id="gates" tabindex="-1">Gates <a class="header-anchor" href="#gates" aria-label="Permalink to “Gates”">​</a></h2><p>ruff check/format clean on the shipped source; <code>ty</code> clean; vulture / lint-imports / bandit / semgrep clean; radon ratchet&#39;s only deltas pre-existing baseline drift (verified identical on stashed main). Tests: <code>test_opmeta</code> projections + single-source pin, <code>_folds_to_param</code> on the <code>rsqrt</code> weight spelling, <code>dag_cost</code> at zero, <code>test_construction_gaps</code> retargeted; dev lane (<code>-m &quot;not slow&quot;</code>) run logged in GOALS.</p>`,22)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};